  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) workshops for judges on Gender Based Violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a series of projects in collaboration with the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC).The first project has started in 2022, in which the UNODC aims to train 180 Egyptian judges of First Instance to enhance their technical capacities, in order to improve the access to justice for women. Whereas, that project predominantly focuses on Gender Based Violence (GBV), this project widens it scope by also focusing on people with disabilities. Considering that both, women and people with disabilities, face obstacles to access the judicial system.This project aims to train 7 to 10 Egyptian judges, by showcasing Dutch regulatory mechanisms and procedures and experiences. Aiming to provide the Egyptian judges know-how on efficient interagency coordination to support women and people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
